## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical lightweight baseline building for text routing under strict latency constraints, in a data-scarce regime with model calibration requirements. Also covers drift monitoring and retraining cadence.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight text representation with a fixed 30-feature vector
- SGD-based multiclass logistic regression or tiny decision tree for efficiency
- Calibration via temperature scaling
- Drift detection using rolling holdout validation
- Deployment latency and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Training loop outline for SGD multiclass LR
const model = new SGDLogisticRegression({
  learningRate: 0.01,
  epochs: 100,
  batchSize: 32
});
model.fit(XTrain, yTrain);
// Temperature scaling for calibration
const temp = calibrateTemperature(model, XVal, yVal);
// Inference
const predict = (features) => {
  const start = performance.now();
  const probs = model.predictProb(features, temp);
  const latency = performance.now() - start;
  return { probs, latency };
};
```

